{"name":"Honest","hex":"#9bb8e2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"honest","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Scrupulous with regard to telling the truth; not given to swindling, lying, or fraud; upright.","True, especially as far as is known by the person making the statement; fair; unbiased."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To adorn or grace; to honour; to make becoming, appropriate, or honourable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Honest (Future album)","blocks":[{"text":"Honest is the second studio album by American rapper Future. It was released on April 22, 2014, through A1 Recordings and Freebandz, and distributed by Epic Records. The album features guest appearances from Pharrell, Pusha T, Casino, Wiz Khalifa, Kanye West, Drake, Young Scooter, André 3000, and Lil Wayne. It was supported by five singles: \"Karate Chop\", \"Honest\", \"Shit\", \"Move That Dope\", and \"I Won\", along with the promotional single, \"Real and True\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/21/Future_Honest_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honest_(Future_album)","wikidata":"Q5893251"},{"title":"Honesty","blocks":[{"text":"Honesty or truthfulness is a facet of moral character that connotes positive and virtuous attributes such as integrity, truthfulness, straightforwardness, along with the absence of lying, cheating, theft, etc. Honesty also involves being trustworthy, loyal, fair, and sincere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Diogenes_looking_for_a_man_-_attributed_to_JHW_Tischbein.jpg/330px-Diogenes_looking_for_a_man_-_attributed_to_JHW_Tischbein.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honesty","wikidata":"Q337349"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com